{#
settings/_insights.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
One row per insight extractor, straight off the registry.

The list is SettingsController::insightsSectionData() mapping
InsightExtractorRegistry::all(), which is the whole point: an extractor added
next release appears here without this template changing. Name and hint are
resolved from the key — `settings.insights.extractor.<key>` and `…<key>_hint`,
the contract InsightExtractorInterface::icon() documents — so shipping an
extractor means shipping its two catalogue lines, nothing here. An extractor
whose lines are missing falls back to its capitalised key rather than showing
the raw catalogue path: the test container registers one such, and a raw key
on a settings page reads as a broken build.

An On/Off SEGMENT rather than a checkbox — the appearance page's idiom, where
every boolean wears the same two-segment control with words on it. Each change
POSTs on its own (settings--insights) and the page never reloads; on a failed
POST the controller puts the previous segment back, because a control showing
a state the server refused is a settings page lying about the setting.

Variables:
  insightExtractors  list of { key, icon, enabled } — enabled is THIS user's
                     answer, from InsightExtractorRegistry::isEnabledFor()
#}
{% set segGroup = 'grid grid-flow-col auto-cols-fr w-28 shrink-0 rounded-pane border border-line overflow-hidden' %}
{% set segText  = 'flex h-full items-center justify-center px-2 py-1.5 text-center text-[11px] leading-tight text-ink-muted
                   peer-checked:bg-accent peer-checked:text-accent-ink
                   peer-focus-visible:ring-2 peer-focus-visible:ring-inset peer-focus-visible:ring-accent
                   transition-colors' %}

<div class="px-4 py-3 space-y-3"
     data-controller="settings--insights"
     data-settings--insights-url-value="{{ path('app_settings_insights_toggle') }}"
     data-settings--insights-token-value="{{ csrf_token('insights_toggle') }}">

    {#
    The strip above the mail list. Not an extractor and not in the loop below,
    because it is not a SOURCE — it is a region. Its own row rather than a
    section of its own, so the one page about insights holds every insight
    switch; the hint carries the distinction, since a reader who has just read
    eight rows that each stop a kind of card being found would otherwise read
    this one the same way.

    The state is read straight off the user rather than passed in like
    insightExtractors: SettingsController::insightsSectionData() maps the
    extractor registry, and there is no registry entry to map for this. Adding
    one variable there to carry one boolean the template can already see would
    be a hop with no decision in it.

    It posts through the same controller and the same token as every row below,
    with the reserved key InsightSettingsController::PANE_KEY.
    #}
    {% set paneKey = constant('App\\Controller\\Settings\\InsightSettingsController::PANE_KEY') %}
    {% set paneOn  = app.user.getSetting(constant('App\\Entity\\User\\User::SETTING_INSIGHT_PANE_DISABLED'), false) != true %}
    {# NOT `data-insight-extractor` — that attribute is the registry's census,
       and InsightSettingsTest counts it against InsightExtractorRegistry::all().
       This row is a region, not a source, and must not be counted as one. #}
    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3" data-insight-pane-switch>
        <span class="flex items-start gap-3 min-w-0">
            <i class="fa-regular fa-rectangle-list w-4 text-zinc-400 mt-0.5 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <span class="min-w-0">
                <span class="block text-xs font-medium text-ink-muted">{{ 'settings.insights.pane'|trans }}</span>
                <span class="block text-[11px] text-ink-faint mt-0.5">{{ 'settings.insights.pane_hint'|trans }}</span>
            </span>
        </span>
        <div class="{{ segGroup }}" role="radiogroup" aria-label="{{ 'settings.insights.pane'|trans }}">
            {% for on in [true, false] %}
                <label class="cursor-pointer">
                    <input type="radio" name="insight-{{ paneKey }}" class="peer sr-only"
                           value="{{ on ? '1' : '0' }}"
                           data-key="{{ paneKey }}"
                           data-action="change->settings--insights#toggle"
                           aria-label="{{ (on ? 'settings.insights.seg.on' : 'settings.insights.seg.off')|trans }}"
                        {{ paneOn == on ? 'checked' : '' }}>
                    <span class="{{ segText }}">
                        {{ (on ? 'settings.insights.seg.on' : 'settings.insights.seg.off')|trans }}
                    </span>
                </label>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>

    {% for extractor in insightExtractors %}
        {% set nameKey = 'settings.insights.extractor.' ~ extractor.key %}
        {% set name = nameKey|trans %}
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"
             data-insight-extractor="{{ extractor.key }}">
            <span class="flex items-start gap-3 min-w-0">
                <i class="{{ extractor.icon }} w-4 text-zinc-400 mt-0.5 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                <span class="min-w-0">
                    <span class="block text-xs font-medium text-ink-muted">{{ name == nameKey ? extractor.key|capitalize : name }}</span>
                    {% set hint = (nameKey ~ '_hint')|trans %}
                    {% if hint != nameKey ~ '_hint' %}
                        <span class="block text-[11px] text-ink-faint mt-0.5">{{ hint }}</span>
                    {% endif %}
                </span>
            </span>
            <div class="{{ segGroup }}" role="radiogroup" aria-label="{{ name == nameKey ? extractor.key|capitalize : name }}">
                {% for on in [true, false] %}
                    <label class="cursor-pointer">
                        <input type="radio" name="insight-{{ extractor.key }}" class="peer sr-only"
                               value="{{ on ? '1' : '0' }}"
                               data-key="{{ extractor.key }}"
                               data-action="change->settings--insights#toggle"
                               aria-label="{{ (on ? 'settings.insights.seg.on' : 'settings.insights.seg.off')|trans }}"
                            {{ extractor.enabled == on ? 'checked' : '' }}>
                        <span class="{{ segText }}">
                            {{ (on ? 'settings.insights.seg.on' : 'settings.insights.seg.off')|trans }}
                        </span>
                    </label>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
        </div>
    {% endfor %}
</div>
